# Factions and reputation (design/data/factions.toml, rep/*.js). `ttl rep expect <bot> <faction> <field> <value>`
# prints "ttl: ..." when it does not hold, which `server.sh test-all` counts as a failure.
# A: Craft-heavy soul, reborn as a dwarf -> Dwargon friendly (dwarf 20 + craft 10); a -80 slap makes it Hostile and
#    the stages follow (only one band stage at a time); clamping at +-100; decay toward 0.
# B: a Dark soul reborn as an orc -> Orc Horde friendly or better, the hidden Outcast Society at 20.
# C: the real rebirth flow as a slime -> Tempest friendly (slime 20), everything else neutral; Exalted is announced once.
# Renown (a worth score from tier, bosses, reputation bands, uniques, bonus): `ttl rep renown`, `expect <bot> renown ...`.
# Expect in the log: "[ttl] rep: TtlBotRepA dwargon -80 -> -50 (command)" and the seed lines "seed dwarf: dwargon=30".
# Also check in game (not asserted here): `tensura get stat TtlBotRepA reputation` follows Dwargon (mirror), and
# an Easy NPC tagged ttl.npc.dwargon killed by a Life 2 player costs 15 (guards.js, see its header).
ttlbot spawn TtlBotRepA
ttlbot spawn TtlBotRepB
ttlbot spawn TtlBotRepC
@sleep 2
# A: 20 ancient debris x 5 = 100 raw Craft karma (score > 100), then death.
ttl karma TtlBotRepA set ancient_debris 20
kill TtlBotRepA
# B: a short life that ended in eight murdered villagers (karma.rcon: dark = true).
ttl karma TtlBotRepB set play_time 216000
ttl karma TtlBotRepB set mob_kills 60
ttl karma TtlBotRepB set villagers 8
ttl karma TtlBotRepB set advancements 10
ttl karma TtlBotRepB expect dark true
kill TtlBotRepB
@sleep 1
ttl karma TtlBotRepA expect phase corridor
ttl karma TtlBotRepB expect phase corridor
# A: seeding as a dwarf.
ttl rep seed TtlBotRepA dwarf
ttl rep list TtlBotRepA
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepA dwargon value 30
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepA dwargon band friendly
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepA dwargon stage friendly
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepA dwargon nostage neutral
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepA dwargon nostage hostile
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepA dwargon score 30
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepA tempest band neutral
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepA tempest stage neutral
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepA falmuth value 0
# A: a -80 slap: Hostile, and only the hostile stage is left.
ttl rep add TtlBotRepA dwargon -80
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepA dwargon value -50
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepA dwargon band hostile
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepA dwargon stage hostile
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepA dwargon nostage friendly
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepA dwargon score -50
# A: band edges (friendly >= 20, honored >= 50, exalted >= 80, unfriendly <= -20) and the clamp.
ttl rep set TtlBotRepA dwargon -20
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepA dwargon band unfriendly
ttl rep set TtlBotRepA dwargon -19
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepA dwargon band neutral
ttl rep set TtlBotRepA dwargon 20
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepA dwargon band friendly
ttl rep set TtlBotRepA dwargon 50
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepA dwargon band honored
ttl rep set TtlBotRepA dwargon 80
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepA dwargon band exalted
ttl rep add TtlBotRepA dwargon 500
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepA dwargon value 100
ttl rep add TtlBotRepA dwargon -900
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepA dwargon value -100
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepA dwargon stage hostile
# A: one decay step is 2 points toward 0 for Dwargon; it never crosses 0.
ttl rep set TtlBotRepA dwargon 30
ttl rep decay TtlBotRepA 1
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepA dwargon value 28
ttl rep set TtlBotRepA blumund -1
ttl rep decay TtlBotRepA 1
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepA blumund value 0
# B: seeded as an orc: Orc Horde (orc 20 + Chaos 15 x score/100, score >= 60) and the hidden Outcast Society.
ttl rep seed TtlBotRepB orc
ttl rep list TtlBotRepB
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepB orc_horde min 29
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepB orc_horde stage friendly
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepB outcast value 20
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepB outcast stage friendly
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepB dwargon value 0
# C: the rebirth hook. A fresh soul is offered Slime; as a slime it starts Tempest friendly.
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepC tempest value 0
kill TtlBotRepC
@sleep 1
execute as TtlBotRepC run ttl wish knowledge
execute as TtlBotRepC run ttl choose slime
ttl karma TtlBotRepC expect phase life2
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepC tempest value 20
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepC tempest band friendly
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepC tempest stage friendly
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepC dwargon value 0
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepC outcast value 0
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepC holy_church band neutral
# C: reaching Exalted announces it once (Voice line in chat; bots never reach Discord).
ttl rep set TtlBotRepC tempest 90
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepC tempest band exalted
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepC tempest stage exalted
ttl rep set TtlBotRepC tempest 10
ttl rep set TtlBotRepC tempest 90
ttl rep log 8
# C: renown (factions.toml [renown]): a fresh underdog soul has tier 0, Tempest friendly is +3, no boss yet.
# The unique it was drawn adds an unknown amount (rarity), so only the parts and lower bounds are asserted.
ttl rep renown TtlBotRepC
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepC renown tier 0
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepC renown rep 15
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepC renown bosses 0
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepC renown bonus 0
# Tempest is exalted here (+15, set above). Bonus renown (quests, merit) and a boss stage (+10 for ttl.boss.t1) add up.
ttl rep bonus TtlBotRepC 7
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepC renown bonus 7
kubejs stages add TtlBotRepC ttl.boss.t1
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepC renown bosses 10
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepC renown min 32
kubejs stages remove TtlBotRepC ttl.boss.t1
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepC renown bosses 0
ttl rep bonus TtlBotRepC -7
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepC renown bonus 0
# Souls still in the Spirit Corridor have no bosses or uniques yet: A's renown has no bonus and no stage points.
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepA renown bonus 0
ttl rep expect TtlBotRepA renown uniques 0
# The player's own view works too.
execute as TtlBotRepC run ttl rep
execute as TtlBotRepC run ttl rep renown
ttl reset TtlBotRepA
ttl reset TtlBotRepB
ttl reset TtlBotRepC
ttlbot remove TtlBotRepA
ttlbot remove TtlBotRepB
ttlbot remove TtlBotRepC
